[{:adr/consequences "{:no_behavior_change \"name-only renames + mechanical deps.edn coordinate updates; internal\\n                       Clojure namespaces (vrm.parse etc.) unchanged -- repo name and\\n                       namespace name are independent concepts (ADR-2607051200 precedent)\", :dependents_updated \"13 dependent repos correctly reference the renamed coordinates\", :scope_discipline \"json/dag-cbor/openapi and ~40 other investigated-and-excluded repos\\n                     intentionally left alone this round\", :process_reinforcement \"two real repo-state surprises reinforce standing practice\\n                          (CLAUDE.md, git-cleanup-conflict skill): always fetch and diff\\n                          against the true remote tip, never assume a shared checkout's\\n                          local HEAD is current, verify the actual pushed commit's diff\\n                          before moving to the next repo -- especially with git reset\\n                          --soft, which does not reset the working tree or catch stale\\n                          index entries\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["9 kotoba-lang repos renamed to reverse-domain external-spec names: atproto->\n    org-bluesky-atproto, ipld->io-ipld, bpmn->org-omg-bpmn, cmmn->org-omg-cmmn,\n    dmn->org-omg-dmn, ical->org-ietf-ical, mcp->org-anthropic-mcp,\n    multiformats->io-multiformats, vrm->org-vrmc-vrm -- each verified genuine (real\n    graph/model/interpreter, not just types) by reading actual README/ADR content before\n    renaming, per ADR-2607052300's own caution about overclaiming spec conformance" "13 dependent repos' deps.edn updated to the new coordinates: vrm dependents\n    (network-isekai, net-babiniku, kami-gen-procedural, kami-gen-ml3d, dance,\n    kami-app-character-creator, kami-gen-hybrid), multiformats dependents (prolly-tree,\n    kami-nv-compat, checkpointer, ipld-itself), ipld dependents (arrangement, chain\n    [formerly commit-dag], kotoba-client, prolly-tree)" "3 medium-confidence candidates (json, dag-cbor, openapi) deliberately NOT renamed this\n    round -- weaker fit to the org-<body>-<spec> shape (json's README never cites RFC 8259\n    by name; dag-cbor is an explicitly partial RFC 8949 profile; OpenAPI Initiative isn't a\n    w3/ietf-style formal body)" "~40 other repos investigated by the audit and excluded entirely -- the\n    card/swift/webrtc/etc 'capability library' family and the RDF/linked-data family all\n    self-disclaim full spec conformance in their own README/ADR" "3 stale manifest/west.yml entries removed as pure hygiene (gltf/glb/usd) -- these repos\n    were already renamed on GitHub to org-khronos-gltf/org-khronos-glb/org-openusd earlier,\n    but the old duplicate manifest entries were never cleaned up" "two real repo-state surprises caught mid-operation and fixed: (1) a git reset --soft\n    mistake on arrangement accidentally reverted an unrelated ADR-citation fix already on\n    the true remote tip, caught and fixed with an immediate follow-up commit; (2) commit-dag\n    had already been renamed to chain by a separate concurrent session (ADR-2607050800) with\n    a real content restructure, detected via a repo-name/content mismatch and fixed via a\n    direct GitHub Contents API edit against the real current repo instead of trusting the\n    stale local checkout"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-rename-batch2", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607052300-kotoba-lang-turn-rt-net-signal-reverse-domain-rename.md" "90-docs/adr/2607051200-kotoba-lang-ui-family-rename.md"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607060100-kotoba-lang-reverse-domain-rename-batch2", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-06", :adr/decision "{:renames [{:old \"atproto\", :new \"org-bluesky-atproto\", :spec \"AT Protocol (Bluesky)\", :dependents []} {:old \"ipld\", :new \"io-ipld\", :spec \"IPLD DAG-CBOR (tag-42 link discipline)\", :dependents [\"arrangement\" \"prolly-tree\" \"chain (formerly commit-dag)\" \"kotoba-client\"]} {:old \"bpmn\", :new \"org-omg-bpmn\", :spec \"BPMN 2.0 (OMG)\", :dependents []} {:old \"cmmn\", :new \"org-omg-cmmn\", :spec \"CMMN 1.1 (OMG)\", :dependents []} {:old \"dmn\", :new \"org-omg-dmn\", :spec \"DMN 1.4 (OMG)\", :dependents []} {:old \"ical\", :new \"org-ietf-ical\", :spec \"iCalendar RFC 5545 (IETF)\", :dependents []} {:old \"mcp\", :new \"org-anthropic-mcp\", :spec \"Model Context Protocol (Anthropic)\", :dependents [\"kotodama-mcp\"]} {:old \"multiformats\", :new \"io-multiformats\", :spec \"multiformats (multihash/CID), verified byte-identical to real go-ipfs/kubo output\", :dependents [\"prolly-tree\" \"kami-nv-compat\" \"checkpointer\" \"io-ipld (itself)\"]} {:old \"vrm\", :new \"org-vrmc-vrm\", :spec \"VRM 1.0 (VRM Consortium)\", :dependents [\"network-isekai\" \"net-babiniku\" \"kami-gen-procedural\" \"kami-gen-ml3d\" \"dance\" \"kami-app-character-creator\" \"kami-gen-hybrid\"]}], :deliberately_not_renamed {:medium_confidence [\"json (RFC 8259 not cited by name)\" \"dag-cbor (explicitly partial RFC 8949 profile)\" \"openapi (OpenAPI Initiative isn't a w3/ietf-style formal body)\"], :excluded_family [\"card/swift/webrtc/banking/securities/treasury/insurance/logistics/\\n                      retail/labor/phone/ip/pkg/groot/cnc/fea/giemon capability-library\\n                      family -- self-disclaim 'models records, not wire format'\" \"rdf/sparql/turtle/n-quads/did/vc/activitypub/activitystreams/\\n                      rdf-canon/shacl/json-ld -- each self-disclaims full conformance\"]}, :manifest_hygiene {:what \"removed 3 stale west.yml entries (gltf/glb/usd) pointing at nonexistent local\\n          paths -- already renamed on GitHub to org-khronos-gltf/org-khronos-glb/\\n          org-openusd earlier, old manifest entries never cleaned up\", :cause \"gen-west-manifest.cljs's --entry flag only adds/replaces, never deletes -- same\\n           caveat noted in ADR-2607051200 and ADR-2607052300\"}, :execution {:steps [\"gh repo rename x9, GitHub preserves redirects\" \"local checkout moved + remote retargeted x9\" \"13 dependent deps.edn updates, each its own single-purpose commit\" \"manifest/repos.edn: 9 :path-overrides + 9 :extra-projects updates, API\\n            single-entry commit\" \"manifest/west.yml: 9 new + 9 removed + 3 stale removed, surgical diff against\\n            GitHub tip via API (whole-file gen blocked by 4 unrelated pre-existing\\n            pin-drift repos: browser/cssom/dom-gpu/htmldom, not this batch's concern)\"], :mistakes_caught_and_fixed [\"network-isekai/net-babiniku had real unrelated uncommitted WIP (a live-streaming\\n     broadcast feature) -- committed ONLY deps.edn in each, left the WIP files exactly as\\n     they were\" \"arrangement: git reset --soft left a stale README.md line staged (pre-fix ADR citation\\n     2607050600 vs the tip's corrected 2607050700), accidentally reverting that fix on push\\n     -- caught by inspecting the pushed commit's diff, fixed with an immediate follow-up\\n     commit, verified git diff against remote showed zero difference afterward. Corrected\\n     procedure for all subsequent repos: `git checkout <true-tip> -- .` (resets both index\\n     AND working tree) before reapplying the one-line edit\" \"quad-store: already merged into arrangement by an earlier, unrelated rename\\n     (ADR-2607050700) -- detected via matching remote-tip SHAs between two supposedly\\n     different local checkouts, confirmed via gh api; left the stale local dir alone, no\\n     separate action needed since arrangement's own fix covers it\" \"commit-dag: already renamed to chain by a separate concurrent session\\n     (ADR-2607050800) with a real content restructure -- detected via repo-name/content\\n     mismatch on diff, fixed via direct GitHub Contents API edit against the real current\\n     repo (chain), then resynced the local directory name\" \"kotodama-mcp's fetch showed '(forced update)' -- verified via gh api compare\\n     (ahead_by:2, behind_by:0) it was a pure fast-forward, not a real force-push, per the\\n     CLAUDE.md shallow-clone false-positive pattern, before proceeding\"]}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"follow-up audit requested after ADR-2607052300: which other kotoba-lang repos\\n           have bare names that plausibly port a specific external spec but aren't yet\\n           reverse-domain named?\", :investigated [\"background agent scanned ~1200 non-compat-catalog kotoba-lang west.yml entries, read\\n    each plausible candidate's actual README/ADR (not name-pattern guessing), reported 12\\n    candidates at varying confidence + a manifest hygiene issue\" \"owner selected: 9 high-confidence candidates (5 no-dependent, 4 with-dependent) +\\n    the hygiene cleanup; explicitly did NOT select the 3 medium-confidence candidates\\n    (json/dag-cbor/openapi)\" \"each of the 9 verified genuine before renaming: bpmn/cmmn/dmn each ship a real\\n    graph/plan-item/decision-table model plus an interpreter, not just types; vrm's README\\n    documents a full 1:1 restoration from a deleted Rust crate (17 namespaces, ~2650 lines,\\n    116 ported test assertions); mcp implements real JSON-RPC method names/error codes at\\n    the manifest/message layer (no transport -- honest scoping, not a disclaimer);\\n    multiformats verified byte-identical to real go-ipfs/kubo output\" \"multiformats renamed before ipld since ipld itself depends on multiformats --\\n    dependency-order care, same principle as always fixing dependents before renaming the\\n    next node up the graph\"], :risk \"same as ADR-2607052300: a repo name overclaiming spec conformance it doesn't have\\n         is worse than a boring bare name\"}", :adr/alternatives [], :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607060100: kotoba-lang -- reverse-domain external-spec rename, batch 2\n          (atproto/ipld/bpmn/cmmn/dmn/ical/mcp/multiformats/vrm)"}]